# Line endings, at the Git level.
#
# .editorconfig is CRLF, which is right for every file a person edits. It is
# wrong for `gradlew`: a shell script with CRLF endings does not run on the
# Linux CI runner. This file reaches Git itself, so the checkout is correct
# however a contributor has `core.autocrlf` set.

* text=auto

# Generated by Gradle and executed by the CI runner. Must stay LF.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts. Must stay CRLF.
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries Git must not touch. gradle-wrapper.jar is committed on purpose: it is
# what lets `./gradlew` bootstrap on a machine with no Gradle installed.
*.jar binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
